- captaind supports a single CLN node
  If captaind manages multiple nodes, finish pending outgoing payments and
  settle or cancel outstanding hold invoices on each node you plan to retire.
  captaind tracks those payments and invoices by the node that created them.

  Save the old config and environment settings before upgrading. captaind
  refuses to start with `[[cln_array]]`. Migrate the node you want to keep.
  - Rename `[[cln_array]]` to `[cln]`.
  - Remove the `priority` field.
  - Replace the JSON env var `BARK_SERVER__CLN_ARRAY` with one env var per
    field, for example `BARK_SERVER__CLN__URI` and
    `BARK_SERVER__CLN__HOLD_INVOICE__URI`.

  If you roll back to Scuttle RC8, restore the old settings with the binary.
  RC8 accepts a config with only `[cln]` and starts without a Lightning node.
  After restarting captaind, verify that the configured node is online.

  ```toml
  [cln]
  uri = "https://cln:9736"
  server_cert_path = "/data/cln/regtest/ca.pem"
  client_cert_path = "/data/cln/regtest/client.pem"
  client_key_path = "/data/cln/regtest/client-key.pem"
  hold_invoice.uri = "https://cln:9988"
  hold_invoice.server_cert_path = "/data/cln/regtest/hold/ca.pem"
  hold_invoice.client_cert_path = "/data/cln/regtest/hold/client.pem"
  hold_invoice.client_key_path = "/data/cln/regtest/hold/client-key.pem"
  ```
